{"diagnosis": "Trace ends with TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Expected mem lookahead address to be 4-byte aligned with low bits 2'b00, but picorv32.v:382 forces 2'b10 in both fetch and data branches. Root cause is hardcoded {..,2'b10} suffix in mem_la_addr at picorv32.v:382, making every fetch misaligned.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -382 +382 @@
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};", "expected": "tohost PASS (no TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero, no FAIL 0xdead)"}

